    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=\\dfrac{-1\\pm\\sqrt2}{2}$.\n\nUse the quadratic formula and simplify $\\sqrt{32}=4\\sqrt2$.",
      "worked": "Use the quadratic formula with $a=4$, $b=4$ and $c=-1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{-4\\pm\\sqrt{4^2-4(4)(-1)}}{2(4)}\\\\x&=\\frac{-4\\pm\\sqrt{32}}{8}\\\\x&=\\frac{-4\\pm4\\sqrt2}{8}\\\\x&=\\frac{-1\\pm\\sqrt2}{2}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
